  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 2 December 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nImagine living this close to the beach, with views across St Heliers Bay and Rangitoto from your own home.\r\n\r\nWelcome to 12 Auckland Road.\r\n\r\nDistinctive from the street and exceptional inside, this home was stripped back to its solid concrete masonry bones and completely rebuilt, with a new Colorsteel roof, full double glazing and a beautifully considered interior.\r\n\r\nWarm timber detailing, a crisp white kitchen and generous open-plan spaces give the home a fresh, sophisticated feel. Windows and balconies have been positioned to capture the water, the village and the ever-changing coastal outlook. \r\n\r\nAcross 257m², there are four bedrooms, three-and-a-half bathrooms and three separate living areas.\r\n\r\nFor families, it offers something increasingly difficult to find: space for everyone without losing the ability to come together.\r\n\r\nFor those with teenagers, extended family or regular guests, the semi-self-contained lower level creates genuine independence and flexibility.\r\n\r\nAnd for busy professionals wanting the St Heliers lifestyle without a large property to maintain, this is an easy home to lock, leave and enjoy.\r\n\r\nThere’s also a double internal-access garage, additional off-street parking and, incredibly, the beach is only around two minutes away.\r\n\r\nStart the day with a swim, walk into the village for coffee, or head down for dinner and leave the car at home.\r\n\r\nFreehold, beautifully reimagined and positioned in the heart of one of Auckland’s most desirable coastal neighbourhoods.\r\n\r\nWhatever stage of life you’re at, this is a home that gives you more options and a lot more time to enjoy them.\r\n\r\nWelcome home.",
